    lifespanDatingNotes:
      "Present at Stephen's stoning as 'a young man' (Acts 7:58), suggesting a birth in the early first century AD, and later calling himself 'Paul, the aged' in a letter written around AD 60 (Philemon 9). Tradition holds he was beheaded in Rome under Nero (as a Roman citizen, exempt from crucifixion) — an account already assumed as common knowledge in 1 Clement, written barely a generation later around AD 96, making this one of the earliest-attested apostolic deaths outside Scripture.",
    tier: "major",
