      "Traditionally the youngest of the Twelve and the only apostle believed to have died a natural death, in old age at Ephesus. Exiled to Patmos under Domitian around AD 95, where he received the visions recorded in Revelation (Revelation 1:9). His long life is attested by Irenaeus, who as a young man had known Polycarp, a direct disciple of John.",
