    noExtraBiblicalRecordNote: "No contemporary extra-biblical historical source mentions Mary Magdalene. Later traditions about her later life — including legends that she traveled to southern France — developed from the medieval period onward and are not historically verifiable. A 2nd-to-4th-century Gnostic text known as the Gospel of Mary, discovered in the 19th century, presents a Mary (widely though not universally identified as Mary Magdalene) as a prominent visionary figure, but it is a later Gnostic religious composition, not a historical record of her life.",
