      "Became king at 30 and reigned 40 years total (2 Samuel 5:4), dying at 70. David's historicity, once doubted by more skeptical scholars, was strikingly confirmed in 1993 when archaeologists at Tel Dan uncovered a 9th-century BC inscription referring to the 'House of David' — a welcome case of the spade backing up the text.",
