      "Bathsheba is introduced as the wife of Uriah the Hittite, one of David's own elite soldiers, and the daughter of Eliam, himself likely one of David's 'mighty men' (2 Samuel 11:3; 23:34), meaning she was already connected to David's inner circle. While Uriah and the army were away besieging Rabbah, David saw her bathing from his rooftop, sent for her, and slept with her; she subsequently sent word that she was pregnant (2 Samuel 11:2-5).",
