      "Cupbearer to Artaxerxes I who traveled to Jerusalem in the king's 20th year, 445 BC (Nehemiah 2:1), to rebuild the walls, later returning for a second term around 433 BC (Nehemiah 13:6-7). These Persian regnal-year references make 445 BC one of the most solidly fixed dates in the Old Testament; his birth and death years aren't recorded.",
